    "result_text": "The full test suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`. (The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit so that creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges, all following the existing `CityCapacityExceededException` pattern in the codebase:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` thrown when the day's create limit is exhausted.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` to `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429), rendered as a `ProblemDetail` like the other business-rule handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `rejectDailyLimitExceeded()`, invoked as the final rule in `prepareNewOwner(...)`. It counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count reaches the `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT` (100).\n\nThe rule sits alongside the existing intake rules (duplicate telephone/household, city capacity), so it applies to the single `POST /api/owners` creation path.",
